+# H35 separate read-only milestone reviews
+
+Finder and skeptic independently accept the H35 evidence. Neither used Lean, a server, builds or edits. Both verified the fresh four-module build, four kernel checks,28 guarded pins and explicit inventory, compiler pipelines, resource bounds and unchanged helper sources. Both independently matched all12 archive artifacts to actual source-cache bytes, hashes/sizes, four traces and input mappings, and the archive SHA256/294765-byte size.
+
+Both confirmed the missing coordinator registry/catalogue/vmexec, actual standard-script role, failed dry-run before transport, absence of a successful receipt/shipped marker and accurate prepared-versus-delivered distinction. No theorem, premise, budget, import, scope or dependency-closure claim changed. Both preserve QREG and H35CACHE blockers.
+
+One reproduction defect was fixed during review: run-gates.sh now includes the explicit axiom-inventory command that had already passed separately. Both reviewers accepted this correction; raw evidence was unchanged. No remaining findings. No H35 checkpoint completion is claimed before actual cache delivery/import confirmation.
